# Russian proverbs: без труда, тише едешь
subtitle: "Stones, pots and little fish: what Russian proverbs say word for word, what they really mean, and words for character."
tags: ["russian","russian proverbs","russian sayings","russian culture","russian phrases"]
teaches: ["phrases/proverbs","vocabulary/feelings"]
thumb: "band \"It isn't gods who fire the pots\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Owner and manager in Russian: владелец, руководитель","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/196-russian-owner-manager.cast"}

